Z||000006||84fierotrevor||10-28-2001||04:16 AM||||yeah i got 6.0 but how do i like take the rims off of one picture and put them into my picture ?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Nashco||10-28-2001||05:16 AM||||Read the help section man...it's not something that we could teach ya how to do on the forum!  That's like asking somebody on the internet how to drive...lol!  The key is to find good pictures to start with.  You need a high quality large photo of your car, and a picture of the wheels that you want to put on your car in the same orientation (if your car is at an angle, the wheels need to be at the same angle).  There are ways to get around this, but that stuff is way beyond you at this point.  Just use the toolbox and start fooling around.  Like I said earlier, "It's really not that hard, just takes a little experience with photoshop and some time."  Experience and time...so practice!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||ray b||10-28-2001||01:03 PM||||Adobe will give you a trial copy of 6.0 photoshop on their site for FREE but is a very long download on a dialup.<BR>FREE copy cannot print/export but you can play with it and see if you like it.<BR>LE [lite]versions are way cheaper and even come with some scanner's for free.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
